      "fingerprint": "81ceae74ff2057da1781b436067cdff9d917227147a937e056d6dbf73a7f70ec",
      "kind": "editorial",
      "status": "blocked",
      "issues": [
        "- In Part 4, the complementary pairs list is wrong: it includes a garbled third bullet “= और ≠ के जोड़े जैसे: > और < के साथ = (तीनों मिलकर पूरक — कुछ प्रश्नों में 'A > B या A ≤ B' का जोड़ा)” which incorrectly describes three relations as complementary and gives a mismatched example. → The correct complementary pairs are > & ≤, < & ≥, = & ≠. For Either-Or, when the statement gives ≥, the pair > and = is also considered complementary (covering all possibilities), but this is a special case and should be explained separately."
      ],
